@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] shared-transport-moving-base
Shared rider carry MUST skip its manual movement only when the character is already based on the exact
target moving body. A station floor or another vehicle with the same service owner MUST NOT suppress
the target body's carry and rebasing. An already based rider MUST NOT receive the same movement twice.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] map-landing-trace
A map zone's optional above_m MUST be converted from metres to centimetres; absent or invalid
values MUST retain the 25 m outdoor default. Accepted heights MUST be finite and within 0–60 m.
Travel MUST preserve the chosen height through the client request and authoritative landing,
with the existing epoch, encounter, pending-hit and rate-limit checks intact.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] local-footstep-original-pools
Original is the only footstep sound set (operator 494): footsteps MUST draw from its pools only, with one
shuffle state per surface shared by feet and horse hoof stand-ins, so no sample repeats back to back.
Bone-plant timing, replay suppression, material/canopy detection, speed/landing gain and pitch, and
Original attenuation MUST be preserved. Hoof stand-ins MUST keep their plain playback, untouched by the
human footstep preferences.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] local-audio-preferences-routing
With softening off and full footstep and skate volume, Original MUST keep its existing cue, shuffle, attenuation
and mix; the softening and volume preferences, release defaults included, adjust only per-voice filter and gain on
top of it. The local world's preferences MUST reach its current and late audio-ready local and remote emitters
without replicating them or changing simulation, plant timing, replay or network authority. A retired saved
soundbank choice MUST be ignored and dropped on the next save.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] local-footstep-preferences
Footstep softening and footstep volume MUST default to their release defaults (JapanReleaseDefaults: on, one).
These client-local controls MUST update current and future human footstep/landing
voices, using per-voice filtering and gain without changing
shared waves, plant timing, replay, attenuation or pitch. Hoof stand-ins, skate,
music and master volume MUST remain unaffected. Finished voices MUST auto-destroy;
world/component teardown MUST stop and release only the owned human footstep voices.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] local-skate-preferences
Skate softening and skate volume MUST default to their release defaults (JapanReleaseDefaults: on, one half). These client-local
controls MUST reach current and late audio-ready skate emitters in this world, and MUST leave footsteps, hoof stand-ins, music and master volume unaffected.
Both controls MUST be reachable from the Esc menu's main page; the Skate feel page owns only its own knobs.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:performance] horse-appearance-residency
An accepted appearance change on a locally controlled horse that replaces breed, tack, coat or mask
assets MUST release the old component references and request deferred engine collection with incremental
purging, so trying looks does not wait for the periodic pass. Appearance loading and movement prediction
MUST NOT collect inline. Remote horses, unchanged looks and colour-only changes MUST NOT request collection.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] horse-pivot-clock
Stationary grounded steering MUST animate stepping in its turn direction, with rotation and animation phase
scaled by the same steering magnitude. Pivot presentation MUST derive from existing checkpointed state without
adding wire role IDs. When pivot clips are absent, the horse MAY use its walk clip as a stepping fallback.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] sword-contact-defence
Sword contact MUST resolve at most once per target per swing and MUST observe active windows crossed
between simulation samples. A perfect parry MUST face the contact, last at most 120 ms of the authored
guard window, and deflect at most one contact per attempt, locally and in server defence history.
Guard pressure MUST change only on resolved contacts and decay with the authority world clock;
movement replay MUST NOT reapply pressure, damage or contact counters. NPC hit immunity MUST allow
separate combo cuts while retaining player recovery protection. Projectile damage MUST resolve only
on authority through the shared defence resolver; flight MUST stop at cover and MUST NOT home after release.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] regional-atlas-travel
Every registered teleport and saved marker MUST remain reachable through its existing travel resolver.
Regional filtering MUST NOT mutate the destination registry or infer travel coordinates from artwork.
Artwork and all overlays MUST share their declared world frame. Opening the atlas MUST choose the
player's mapped region, falling back to the world overview outside regional artwork coverage.
Stable names MUST be editable live labels, never baked into paintings. A failed name save MUST preserve
the previous file and in-memory names; pawn switches MUST share the local world's saved names.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] regional-atlas-controller
Every on-sheet destination MUST remain individually selectable with a controller, including coincident
pins. Controller camera pan MUST retain the screen-space reticle away from sheet boundaries. Map focus
MUST consume controller movement instead of driving gameplay. Back MUST return from region to world,
then close the world view; selection MUST use the destination's existing travel resolver.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] remote-vehicle-presentation
Releasing a remote skate pose, including repeated stow or travel after its bone buffer is empty,
MUST restore capsule-relative mesh placement without changing the authoritative capsule. A new activity
epoch MUST discard the previous streamed mesh frame. Listen-host horse visual interpolation MUST NOT
change the authoritative horse checkpoint. Zeppelin passengers MUST follow the rendered ship without
an additional character smoothing offset.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] live-player-map-travel
Online player map targets MUST use session player identity, follow the current pawn, and disappear
when that player leaves. Travel MUST resolve the identity on the host at request time and retain epoch,
encounter, pending-contact and rate admission. A destination MUST have walkable ground and standing
capsule clearance; the chosen floor MUST NOT be replaced by an overhead bridge or roof.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] native-map-tour-diagnostics
Map-tour diagnostics MUST act only on the locally controlled pawn, use ordinary map travel,
and record settled runtime facing, walkable floor and standing capsule clearance without
forcing the accepted position. A requested single zone MUST fail if absent or ambiguous.
Keeping a diagnostic listen-host alive after its tour MUST be explicitly bounded to at most
120 seconds and MUST NOT change normal gameplay or normal tour completion.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] train-vehicle-admission
Deploying a skateboard, carried board, bike, horse or sailboat MUST be refused while
standing or seated aboard a train or during its boarding walk, locally and on the host.
The train gate MUST NOT block stowing an existing vehicle or bypass activity epochs,
pending-contact checks, encounter admission or movement replay protections. Merely
holding a board MUST NOT be advertised or presented as available while on the train.
Owner board, pose and bail-body transport MUST NOT introduce visible boards aboard;
valid hide/stow packets MUST retain existing sequence and rate admission. Retained
board/pose/bail presentation MUST be masked while aboard even without an owner hide packet.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] train-passenger-camera
The train first-person view MUST be local to the viewing player and available only to
standing or seated passengers, never during the boarding walk. Its preference MUST belong
to the local controller and survive pawn replacement without affecting another player.
Body and attached equipment hiding MUST affect only that player's current view, preserve
existing component visibility/ownership, and include attachments added while viewing.
Leaving or losing possession MUST release the train camera; map/menu input MUST NOT toggle
it, and its controller bumper MUST NOT also operate a nearby zeppelin.
Fixed and cinematic views MUST take over immediately without a residual train-camera blend
or hidden passenger body. Suspended controls MUST NOT change the camera preference.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] train-boarding-admission-recovery
Train passenger admission MUST be granted only by completing a station boarding walk on authority,
replicated in the passenger snapshot, preserved across seats, gangway grace and pawn replacement,
and revoked on alighting, cancellation, respawn, map travel, disconnect or expiry outside the train.
Clients MUST NOT grant or revoke admission locally. Unadmitted players carried by a moving or
departing coach MUST be recovered only to verified walkable non-train ground with standing capsule
clearance and a swept floor, never beside a coach in a tunnel or on a viaduct and never via an
unverified fallback teleport. Platform bystanders intersected by a passing coach MUST NOT be relocated.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] racing-service-and-broadcasts
ARacingService MUST own FHRWorldState only on authority, persist world saves atomically
with unreadable/invalid save quarantine rather than silent overwrite, register only the
local host player until guest identity persistence exists, and replicate only the compact
FRacingNetState snapshot (never FHRWorldState::Seed). RacingMotion::Distance, RacingGround::Pick
hit selection and RacingTv::Direct camera selection from the snapshot, shared clock and
spectator positions MUST be deterministic, with zero per-frame network traffic and no silent breed/coat/clip
stand-ins when required assets are missing. Runner gait thresholds, play rates and seat contacts
MUST share UHorseComponent's definitions, and Belmonte TV placements MUST follow the region's
authored building transforms from runtime.json without falling back to hardcoded coordinates.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] release-default-preferences
A fresh install's preferences, a missing saved key and the menus' resets MUST all take the release defaults
(JapanReleaseDefaults, the operator's preset exactly). A saved value MUST still win, except light values that the existing
light_version migration retires from a file saved before the current light. A release default that names no
preference or leaves its range MUST be refused and reported, never clamped or rounded; preferences it does not list
keep their built-in defaults.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] offline-interact-reachability
AWandererCharacter::Interact MUST be a no-op, offline as online, unless a train, zeppelin or sword trainer is in
reach: it MUST NOT set an Interact action or animation state, and it MUST check zeppelin (IsPassenger/CanReach)
and trainer (CanTalk) reachability before Sword->CancelForInterrupt, so a press with nothing in reach never stows
an armed blade or leaves the walker pose stuck.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] transport-audio-from-state
Transport sound (UTransportAudioComponent and its zeppelin, ferry and gondola components) MUST be presentation that
each machine derives from the vehicle's replicated or deterministic state; the zeppelin's comes from the phase, RPM,
gate and landing it already derives from FZeppelinNetworkState or the offline ride. It MUST NOT replicate or change
simulation, timing or authority, and it MUST stay silent without the imported bank or on a dedicated server. Loops
MUST fade towards state-set targets and stop only once inaudible; one-shots MUST fire once per state transition and
never for the state first observed (a late joiner). There is one transport bank, with no alternate soundbanks.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] racing-hud-venue
The race HUD banner MUST be English and MUST appear only inside a venue's grounds near track height.
The broad runner-rendering proximity radius MUST NOT enable the HUD banner.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness;performance] foliage-startup-upload-lifetime
Initial world population MUST bound queued foliage representation uploads after complete source registrations.
A drain MAY wait for GPU completion and retire deferred resources, but MUST preserve GPU render buffers,
source collision, geometry, materials, placements and saved packages. Once gameplay readiness has been
observed, ordinary refreshes and settings toggles MUST NOT introduce GPU-idle drains. Memory diagnostics
MUST distinguish CPU resource estimates from actual process footprint; a source hypothesis is not proof
of a startup memory improvement.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness;performance] foliage-game-vertex-residency
An uncooked non-editor game MAY release CPU vertex copies only for owned prepared render-only
foliage variants after their completed GPU upload. Originals, collision, index arrays, saved packages,
vertex/UV/section metadata and GPU resources MUST remain intact. Editor/PIE, commandlets, CPU-access,
streamable, compiling, pending-upload, Nanite and ray-traced meshes MUST NOT use this path. Later CPU
geometry readers or resource rebuilds MUST NOT use a released variant; use the unchanged original or
the build-time preparation process. Actual physical memory and rendered/toggled gameplay MUST establish
the effect; resource size estimates alone are insufficient.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness;performance] foliage-render-only-collision-residency
Owned prepared foliage render copies MUST NOT retain unused physics meshes or navigation triangle arrays
in an uncooked game. Runtime release MUST require exact mesh ownership of both BodySetup and navigation
data and no pending physics cook, leave original/shared collision and gameplay queries intact, and never
cook, serialize or save mesh packages. Counts, directly allocated navigation bytes and physical footprint
MAY measure this release; physics resource sizing MUST NOT serialize full meshes during startup.
CPU corner readers MUST check GetAllowCPUAccess rather than cached raw pointer non-null after release.
